          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using it as your post-workout protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Bone broth protein is mostly collagen, which is low in leucine and missing tryptophan. A scoop does far less for muscle repair than the same grams of whey, soy or a pea blend. Use Paleovalley as a top-up in coffee or soup, and get your training protein from a complete source.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per tub instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $55 tub sounds similar to a $55 tub of whey, but Paleovalley holds about 390 g of protein against roughly 1,500 g or more in a large whey tub. Always divide price by total grams of protein and multiply by 25 before deciding a product is good value.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Shaking it into cold water</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Because it is a water-simmered broth rather than an acid-hydrolyzed collagen, it does not dissolve as fully as collagen peptides, and the brand says as much. Stir it into warm liquid, use a frother or blend it. Cold shaker bottles are where most texture complaints in buyer reviews come from.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying flavored when you cook savory</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Chocolate and Vanilla are built for coffee and smoothies and contain monk fruit and coconut milk powder. If you plan to use the powder in soups, stews or sauces as well, buy Unflavored. One tub that works everywhere gets used up; a sweet tub often sits in the cupboard.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring sodium and medical conditions</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Broth carries natural sodium and potassium, and a concentrated protein adds to your daily total. That is fine for most people, but anyone with kidney disease, a sodium-restricted diet or a pregnancy should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before making any broth or protein powder a daily habit.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
